  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zam-zam  Foundation</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zamzam Foundation is a non-governmental and not-for-profit organization founded in Mogadishu in 1992 with a mission to provide people affected by human and natural crises in the Horn of Africa with emergency relief, educational programs, clean water and food security, health care, protection for children and orphans, sustainable socio-economic programs, and peace-building and effective governance programs, while integrating our values of respect, impartiality, quality, accountability, advocacy and innovation in all our work. Zamzam have become the largest national humanitarian and development organization in Somalia with almost three decades of experience providing relief and socio-economic support services to those most affected by conflict and recurrent climatic shocks. Zamzam&apos;sheadquarters are in Mogadishu, Somalia, with field operation offices across the country and international offices in Kenya and Turkey.
VISION
Zamzam envisions a day when there is no more poverty in the Horn of Africa and every person&#x2019;s dignity is protected, especially those affected by human and natural crises.
MISSION
To provide people affected by human and natural crises in the Horn of Africa with emergency relief, education, clean water and food security, health care, protection for children and orphans, sustainable socio-economic programs, and to promote peace-building and effective governance.</narrative>
